    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Salesforce Subscribe requires bidirectional streaming. The official grpc/grpc-web client explicitly does not support bidirectional or client-side streaming, so that client cannot directly implement the Subscribe RPC simply by generating browser stubs. This conclusion concerns that client’s supported RPC modes. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:76e0f29d830329969aadf9f9088a4ef2af0fb452a8c7a1afc6675758f568f972",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3c7309f98534e9f9a19b1c0844d167b731e150feea74afcfddae4882ff7069e7",
            "ev:6410beb5ae901fe1ac39eb5594329f399e786ffe80192a6e9bed3d13eb5ba59e",
            "ev:faafdd124db88561e67c7b4d8b762c8c5994a63e5840f64481545d419e2646aa"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/grpc/grpc-web"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Transport compatibility inference for case alerting: Salesforce Subscribe requires bidirectional streaming, so the official gRPC-Web browser client cannot implement that RPC merely by adding its usual proxy. A native gRPC subscriber in a compatible runtime, with a separate browser delivery interface, avoids this particular browser transport mismatch. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1447ac9f2981334e1b4204acdb6e982420850ace97146350b763197492db0c5b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3c7309f98534e9f9a19b1c0844d167b731e150feea74afcfddae4882ff7069e7",
            "ev:6410beb5ae901fe1ac39eb5594329f399e786ffe80192a6e9bed3d13eb5ba59e",
            "ev:8328dd01e8daee5e04040eee956456dd9534e4b975ff0966def61f4d490f7014",
            "ev:faafdd124db88561e67c7b4d8b762c8c5994a63e5840f64481545d419e2646aa"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/grpc/grpc-web",
            "https://github.com/forcedotcom/pub-sub-api"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The official grpc/grpc-web streaming roadmap says full-duplex streaming is not planned and explicitly declines WebSocket full-duplex support. Treat the Improbable WebSocket transport as a separate implementation rather than an official grpc/grpc-web feature. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/grpc/grpc-web/blob/master/doc/streaming-roadmap.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:25c952d54f518cc2fe8c37850b3983f4dbe2629fe03fbc259d6ca9a5e359396a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:285f2bc32b5e00f11db0a5252862ef5a9685f598185fa4b4324438f4a82906c3",
            "ev:2e053784107d115441b11efdfa6dccbce339333b08db411f2629524d44eb8f49",
            "ev:82cfb9921d455671446cc733b4c413ee12f827491cb613087ddbac398e26b218"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/improbable-eng/grpc-web/blob/master/client/grpc-web/docs/transport.md"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Salesforce’s sample repository lists Java, Python, Go, and Node among gRPC client languages and states that a client also needs an Avro library for its chosen language. This is a runtime/library requirement, not a browser compatibility guarantee. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/forcedotcom/pub-sub-api",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:340c40593939c5012d7d769e8cbdce221e7051e9bd2752858b70b5bceb7dd25f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:d1ca340c0db134d1f1197c9f9713587aa738a8572cd89331e340c42111679556"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Salesforce explicitly commits to official support for Java code samples; samples in other languages are not officially supported. The Java samples still require enhancements and functional and performance testing before production deployment. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/other-code-examples.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f7ac13d51878513b9986cd05ebdb0d3ed52a442d0d1011860eb53c2f1ef2d621",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:213833272dfb44c3610a0e020ef54638f79167e2c0c76eba613dc0106bb3e839"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The official grpc/grpc-web browser client connects through a special proxy, defaulting to Envoy. Its supported streaming mode is server-side streaming in grpcwebtext mode; this must not be mistaken for native bidirectional gRPC support. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/grpc/grpc-web",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:39119da785b01a35df2b3d5a50f5d60b481740ccdbb664f14f7753bb9d971a4c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5ba0909b60981f5443dd643406192fb0987fb5c0c66c73cba72a25321c038a1f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The browser restriction is implementation-specific: Improbable’s gRPC-Web client documents a built-in WebSocket transport for client and bidirectional streaming, but requires WebSocket support on its grpc-web-proxy. This is an alternative gateway architecture, not evidence of direct Salesforce browser endpoint compatibility. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/improbable-eng/grpc-web/blob/master/README.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:154051b41ae1f6d1f9b3b51dfa0bf36f287e4051421e5561c5b529f64f4cd207",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a30db7ff0c8fb67a2daf19a0cd0ad8f662a80a462cfb75a8a3feda41580e9cec",
            "ev:cbe29d7e5ae5438f62ae598fc78745acb955da9e2a1989b75e41b01daa5a7b1e",
            "ev:e6eaa6a394f026cc20d430950444744e0c3e47fc5fb5b51e5c9edb83361e95f1"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/improbable-eng/grpc-web/blob/master/client/grpc-web/docs/transport.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pub/Sub API supports multiple client languages through gRPC; Salesforce supplies Java, Python and Go examples, and language selection also requires an Avro library. Language compatibility does not establish official support for every sample. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/other-code-examples.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:795a2379c5daf348f7928de36edb7abdd9a0b95accdaa0c289bb988f0031af23",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2f7ab87399140fff0af35d1b7215d31890cf9736cbffde2874da0be58c7c9dad",
            "ev:49c2e2ad0dd562c1c482d6943508923e52a5ce1983823206f21a71611ba2b2b6",
            "ev:84c9309056da3c3eff9683fc5882849a212a9d0cb53f73761b38dfb26236c71f"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/forcedotcom/pub-sub-api"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Browser gRPC-Web uses a different wire protocol from native gRPC. Its normal deployment translates through a compatible proxy; the official browser client documents Envoy as the default. A browser bundle alone does not supply that translation. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/grpc/grpc/blob/master/doc/PROTOCOL-WEB.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:39a09f54aaf5a11ba2dcbe096ed79174616c88115a5e889725b06c13b75c4099",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:267ba7f30fc7944b008c75c4f180a01639c4592df1a1746ec865a70744761129",
            "ev:e8eade575c7c7709f01e65a1bd5f09fb3c29772b6f254c8fc39f4bdc7d8762fb"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/grpc/grpc-web"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The official gRPC-Web client currently supports unary and server-streaming calls, with server streaming limited to grpcwebtext mode; client-side and bidirectional streaming are unsupported. Its roadmap does not promise full-duplex streaming and explicitly rejects a WebSocket implementation. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/grpc/grpc-web",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e14cc76fcd8a78bfd606b45dfc521b2bf24e87f79b02b0d600b9564c36ccbb05",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:c8e949c43a532344683d94d2ab7b7a94c95411eae6f3fffec0e2d1cd71e6ad10",
            "ev:ca0d15d9207a488909f11618e6baab1c3a3082ef8d862e972e4770889bc53ca9"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/grpc/grpc-web/blob/master/doc/streaming-roadmap.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Improbable’s repository declares maintenance mode and recommends migration to the official gRPC-Web client. Its WebSocket capability therefore needs a maintenance assessment before adoption. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/improbable-eng/grpc-web/blob/master/README.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:00d2061cfc63dc73e9c8a21698bca2fb871701a65cbb7bac8f992d822801a42a",
